{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Validated Memory Ledger.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Validated Memory Ledger.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"validated memory ledger validated memory ledger","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Validated Memory Ledger.md","fileName":"Validated Memory Ledger.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Validated Memory Ledger","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[DevOps Agent Memory and MCP]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Memory and MCP","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Validated Memory Ledger.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Validated Memory Ledger.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"validated memory ledger validated memory ledger","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Validated Memory Ledger.md","fileName":"Validated Memory Ledger.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Validated Memory Ledger","heading":"Validated Memory Ledger","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A validated memory ledger stores approved agent memory in an auditable repository surface such as a dedicated issue. A workflow loads recent valid JSON entries, combines them with current context, lets the model propose a candidate, and writes only entries that pass deterministic checks.\n\nThe ledger demonstrates read and write separation. Existing memory informs a response, but new output does not become durable automatically. Each accepted record can include a timestamp, source pull request, repository scope, value, and reason, making later use inspectable and allowing unsafe or obsolete entries to be corrected.","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Memory and MCP","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Validated Memory Ledger.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Validated Memory Ledger.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"validated memory ledger validated memory ledger","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Validated Memory Ledger.md","fileName":"Validated Memory Ledger.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Validated Memory Ledger","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Memory and MCP","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}